---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import SoundSignatureLab from '../../components/SoundSignatureLab.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title="Sound Signature Lab | Soare Robert Daniel" description="Explore common headphone and IEM sound signatures, then test your gear with tones, noise, and a full frequency sweep." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<section>
				<p class="eyebrow">Headphone and IEM reference tool</p>
				<h1>Sound Signature Lab</h1>
				<div class="divider"></div>
				<p class="intro">See how neutral, bright, dark, warm, cold, and V-shaped tunings distribute energy across the audible range. Then use the generator to check for channel imbalance, rattles, peaks, dips, or missing frequencies in your headphones and IEMs.</p>

				<SoundSignatureLab />

				<div class="guide">
					<div>
						<h2>How to use it</h2>
						<ol>
							<li>Pick a curve to compare the vocabulary people use when describing a headphone's tuning.</li>
							<li>Use a quiet pure tone to investigate a specific frequency, or run a sweep to locate a rattle, resonance, or dropout.</li>
							<li>Use noise to listen for broad tonal balance. These reference curves are illustrative, not measurements of a specific product.</li>
						</ol>
					</div>
					<div class="frequency-guide">
						<h2>Quick frequency guide</h2>
						<p><strong>20–60 Hz:</strong> rumble and sub-bass. <strong>60–250 Hz:</strong> punch and warmth.</p>
						<p><strong>250 Hz–2 kHz:</strong> body, vocals, and instruments. <strong>2–6 kHz:</strong> clarity, attack, and possible harshness.</p>
						<p><strong>6–20 kHz:</strong> sparkle and air. Hearing above 15 kHz varies greatly by person and age.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	:global(main) {
		width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 2rem));
		max-width: none;
		padding-inline: 0;
	}

	.eyebrow {
		margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
		color: var(--accent);
		font-size: 0.72rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.13em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	h1 {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	.intro {
		max-width: 760px;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.guide {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 1rem;
		margin-top: 1rem;
	}

	.guide > div {
		padding: 1.25rem;
		background: var(--bg-card);
		border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
		border-radius: 12px;
	}

	.guide h2 {
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
		font-size: 1rem;
	}

	.guide ol {
		margin: 0;
		padding-left: 1.2rem;
	}

	.guide li,
	.frequency-guide p {
		margin: 0 0 0.55rem;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		line-height: 1.55;
	}

	.frequency-guide p:last-child,
	.guide li:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	.frequency-guide strong {
		color: var(--accent);
	}

	@media (max-width: 680px) {
		:global(main) {
			width: min(100% - 1.5rem, 1180px);
		}

		.guide {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
